# RefIccMAX command-line tools package

This package is a minimal distribution of RefIccMAX command-line tools and the
runtime libraries needed by those tools.

Native packages install into the platform layout:

- `@CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR@` for command-line tools
- `@CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR@` for shared RefIccMAX libraries
- `@CMAKE_INSTALL_DOCDIR@` for package notes, license, version, and tool catalog

Portable archives use the same runtime install component and are intended for
unpack-and-run testing. Build a portable, self-contained archive from a static
configuration (`ENABLE_SHARED_LIBS=OFF`, `ENABLE_STATIC_LIBS=ON`). Build native
`.deb` and `.rpm` packages from a dynamic configuration.

The rolling Linux release ZIP uses the dynamic configuration also used for
DEB/RPM. Its tools locate bundled RefIccMAX libraries through relative install
RPATHs (`$ORIGIN/../lib` and `$ORIGIN`). This ZIP still requires the system
libraries listed in the DEB/RPM dependencies, including compatible libxml2;
it does not bundle every third-party runtime. Release CI extracts the ZIP into
a fresh directory and tests profile dump and XML round-trip without
`LD_LIBRARY_PATH` or `LD_PRELOAD` overrides before upload.

The `Testing/` source tree, man pages, shell completions, and development
headers are intentionally excluded from v1 runtime packages.
